We're updating this post as developments happen.
- Donald Trump has threatened to "obliterate" Iranian energy sites, including Kharg Island, its main oil terminal in the Persian Gulf, if Tehran does not agree a peace deal "shortly";
- In the same Truth Social post, the US president also claimed talks to end the war with a "NEW, AND MORE REASONABLE, REGIME" were making "great progress". The post followed the pattern of Trump's contradictory comments about the status of the war;
- Iran has directly contradicted Trump, saying US demands are "unrealistic, illogical and excessive";
- Oil prices are at a near four-year high, with a barrel of Brent crude costing more than $115;
- Thousands of additional US Marines are set to arrive in the region. American forces are preparing for a ground invasion of Iran, according to the Washington Post, despite domestic opposition and Trump's previous remarks;
- Iran's parliamentary speaker has warned its armed forces are "waiting" for that land arrival - and will punish US partners in the region, while the Iranian army vowed to target the homes of US and Israeli officials;
- Two more UN peacekeepers from Indonesia have been killed in Lebanon after Benjamin Netanyahu announced a widening of Israel's invasion of southern Lebanon as his forces target the Iranian-backed Hezbollah militant group there.
